WEBVTT

00:01.120 --> 00:04.640
♪ Take a walk
To the edge of town ♪

00:04.720 --> 00:07.520
♪ And go across the tracks ♪

00:09.040 --> 00:11.120
♪ Where the viaduct looms ♪

00:11.200 --> 00:13.200
♪ Like a bird of doom ♪

00:13.280 --> 00:17.120
♪ As it shifts and cracks ♪

00:17.640 --> 00:21.440
♪ Where secrets lie
In the border fires ♪

00:21.520 --> 00:23.360
♪ In the humming wires ♪

00:23.440 --> 00:24.520
♪ Hey man, you know ♪

00:24.600 --> 00:27.080
♪ You're never coming back ♪

00:33.800 --> 00:36.240
♪ On a gathering storm comes ♪

00:36.320 --> 00:37.920
♪ A tall handsome man ♪

00:38.000 --> 00:40.320
♪ In a dusty black coat with ♪

00:40.400 --> 00:44.520
♪ A red right hand ♪

01:18.640 --> 01:19.920
[Ada] He's back.

01:21.320 --> 01:22.960
[Michael] Was he out there all night?

01:23.640 --> 01:25.320
Every night since the funeral.

01:25.840 --> 01:28.520
Comes back in the morning to see Charles
and feed the horses,

01:28.600 --> 01:30.840
and when it gets dark, he goes off again.

01:32.520 --> 01:34.360
He used to sleep out when he was a kid.

01:35.840 --> 01:37.720
Curly would find him in the pasture.

01:39.800 --> 01:41.240
How's the baby?

01:42.600 --> 01:44.400
[Ada] He asks for him mum at night.

01:45.560 --> 01:48.120
[clicks tongue] Tommy made a list.

01:48.200 --> 01:49.840
He wants to see you two first.

01:49.920 --> 01:52.200
-What about John and Arthur?
-[door opens]

02:02.200 --> 02:03.200
[door closes]

02:12.320 --> 02:13.480
How are the books?

02:17.240 --> 02:18.240
Unaffected.

02:19.120 --> 02:20.600
Up slightly.

02:23.520 --> 02:25.800
There's also been a threefold increase
in donations

02:25.880 --> 02:27.760
to the Shelby Foundation charity.

02:29.160 --> 02:33.240
The councilor suggested naming the new
school "The Grace Shelby Institute."

02:40.040 --> 02:43.480
Tell the counselor the name "Grace
Shelby Institute" is acceptable to us.

02:43.560 --> 02:44.560
[sniffs]

02:49.600 --> 02:51.960
This is a list on the other things
I want doing.

02:53.480 --> 02:54.640
That's all.

02:56.320 --> 02:57.600
[clears throat]

03:02.640 --> 03:04.080
-Tommy.
-That's all, Pol.

03:14.640 --> 03:16.200
Well done, both of you.

03:25.800 --> 03:27.680
Right, let's go.

03:27.760 --> 03:28.960
Uh, we've already seen him.

03:34.040 --> 03:36.440
He wanted to see people
in a particular order.

03:38.920 --> 03:43.440
I can normally read him, but he's
difficult to read, so be careful.

03:44.960 --> 03:47.240
I thought it was a fucking family meeting.

03:47.480 --> 03:49.080
All of us together, I thought.

03:49.160 --> 03:50.480
John, he's grieving.

03:50.560 --> 03:52.760
To see everyone together
would be too much.

03:53.080 --> 03:56.600
Yeah, well, come on, John.

03:58.240 --> 04:00.040
Arthur, we need him back.

04:01.000 --> 04:05.200
Sabini and Solomons have already sent
condolences and flowers,

04:05.280 --> 04:08.320
so it won't be long before
they come trotting up the A1 like wolves.

04:08.400 --> 04:10.040
Go on. There's a timetable.

04:13.760 --> 04:15.080
[Polly] Only good news.

04:15.480 --> 04:17.200
There is only good news, Polly.

04:19.440 --> 04:20.480
Here we fucking go.

04:21.440 --> 04:24.280
Well, there he is.

04:26.280 --> 04:27.280
Hi, Tom.

04:28.160 --> 04:29.280
Hello, boys.

04:29.720 --> 04:34.840
We, uh, didn't get a chance to see you
after the funeral.

04:35.600 --> 04:39.960
Well, you disappeared on us, but, well,
me and John, we just wanna say that--

04:40.040 --> 04:41.080
Arthur, shut up.

04:41.160 --> 04:42.280
All right.

04:43.520 --> 04:45.040
All right, talk to me.

04:46.000 --> 04:50.080
We got to Angel at the hospital
where he laid. Cut his throat.

04:51.280 --> 04:52.280
He's dead.

04:53.120 --> 04:56.440
Cleared out the rest of the Italians
out of the south of the city.

04:56.520 --> 04:57.920
[John] They mostly went to
the Black Country,

04:58.000 --> 04:59.880
but we told Betty Kitchins
to keep her moving.

04:59.960 --> 05:01.400
And Betty sends her condolences.

05:01.480 --> 05:02.840
What about the old man?

05:03.720 --> 05:05.080
We interrogated his boys.

05:05.160 --> 05:06.680
Yeah, he went to Liverpool.

05:06.760 --> 05:08.480
He's waiting
for an immigrant ship to New York.

05:08.560 --> 05:09.920
When?

05:10.000 --> 05:11.640
Berthed ship sails Saturday.

05:12.760 --> 05:17.680
All right, I have contacts,
people in Cunard and Liverpool.

05:18.480 --> 05:19.520
They'll have passenger lists.

05:19.600 --> 05:21.720
They can get you into the point
of departure.

05:21.800 --> 05:23.480
You pick him up, and you bring him to me.

05:23.600 --> 05:24.920
Who's he got traveling with him?

05:26.520 --> 05:28.320
-His wife.
-What?

05:29.280 --> 05:30.520
His wife.

05:30.600 --> 05:32.360
So shoot her, and bring him to me.

05:37.880 --> 05:41.800
Uh, Tommy, Mrs. Changretta
was a teacher at our school.

05:41.880 --> 05:44.600
She's a good woman, Tom, a good woman.

05:49.640 --> 05:52.600
Well, if she's a good woman,
then she'll go to heaven, eh, Arthur?

05:55.200 --> 05:58.360
[exhales] Just do what's on the list,
nothing else. Then burn it.

05:58.440 --> 06:01.920
Don't speak in the phones.
The fucking Secret Service is listening.

06:03.120 --> 06:04.120
[sighs]

06:05.240 --> 06:08.000
I want the old man alive.
I wanna do it myself.

06:16.280 --> 06:17.920
That's it. [clears throat] You can go.

06:22.720 --> 06:24.160
Come, John.

06:24.240 --> 06:28.920
Tommy, if you haven't got a bird here,
you're gonna have to tell us something.

06:29.120 --> 06:30.520
Ask Polly.

06:32.320 --> 06:33.600
Not Michael?

06:34.080 --> 06:35.080
What?

06:35.400 --> 06:36.840
-Not Michael, no?
-No.

06:36.920 --> 06:39.880
Not Michael, no, 'cause
Michael deals with legitimate business.

06:41.000 --> 06:42.200
You saw him before us.

06:42.280 --> 06:44.640
John, not now.

06:45.080 --> 06:46.240
Wait, what did you say?

06:47.360 --> 06:49.520
You saw Michael before us!

06:49.600 --> 06:50.840
Fuck's sake, John.

06:53.400 --> 06:56.440
Because legitimate business, John,
is the priority.

06:58.440 --> 07:00.720
-Legitimate business--
-Since when?

07:00.800 --> 07:05.560
Since my fucking wife took a bullet
meant for me.

07:10.200 --> 07:12.760
[sniffs] Oh, yeah. Okay.

07:12.840 --> 07:15.480
Yeah, so Secret Service.
Secret fucking Service...

07:15.560 --> 07:18.200
Blah, blah, blah.
But you don't tell us shit.

07:18.280 --> 07:20.920
We're a couple of fucking toy soldiers.

07:21.000 --> 07:24.760
"Do this, John. Do that, John.
Kill your fucking teacher, John!"

07:34.600 --> 07:35.920
This is how it's gonna be.

07:38.440 --> 07:41.760
All right, listen to me.
There's gonna be a little war

07:41.840 --> 07:44.960
in a little place
that no one gives a fuck about.

07:45.480 --> 07:48.560
And the side that is gonna lose
needs a little bit of help.

07:48.760 --> 07:50.440
And they're willing to pay.

07:50.520 --> 07:55.840
When that business is done,
legitimate business is the priority.

07:55.920 --> 07:59.200
Now, do what's on the list and fuck off.

08:02.080 --> 08:03.080
[sniffles]

08:07.880 --> 08:08.880
[exhales]

08:13.360 --> 08:15.360
When are you coming back, hmm?

08:16.200 --> 08:17.400
I'm back, Arthur.

08:28.920 --> 08:30.120
[Arthur] Yeah, well, John,
you're just as young.

08:30.200 --> 08:31.360
[John] Cheers.

08:31.440 --> 08:34.640
The thing is, we all naturally came
in here, where the servants eat.

08:34.720 --> 08:39.000
It's nothing to do with politics, either.
It's fucking freezing in the big room.

08:39.080 --> 08:41.120
John, mind your language in front of Carl.

08:41.200 --> 08:42.960
Ada, we're in the servants' quarters

08:43.040 --> 08:45.880
because it's where the fucking booze
is kept.

08:45.960 --> 08:48.120
-Arthur, find better words!
-Yes.

08:48.200 --> 08:50.000
Pol, does swearing in Gypsy count?

08:50.080 --> 08:53.440
That's no reason for us to be speaking
Rokka or Shelta in any case.

08:53.520 --> 08:55.200
[all exclaiming]

08:55.280 --> 08:57.320
I'm just saying there is no need.

08:57.840 --> 09:00.400
When she's drunk,
my wife can't speak fucking English.

09:00.480 --> 09:01.920
-John!
-Fucking right!

09:05.800 --> 09:07.120
[Polly] You dealt with it?

09:07.200 --> 09:09.400
Incentives, no threats.

09:09.480 --> 09:12.960
Implied consequences without
specific reference to physical harm.

09:13.480 --> 09:16.400
That's why your Michael is the boss.

09:17.080 --> 09:19.760
He knows better words, right, Pol?

09:19.840 --> 09:21.480
Since when was I your boss, Arthur?

09:21.560 --> 09:24.880
First, the boss meets you.
Then the workers meet you.

09:24.960 --> 09:27.200
When did either of you two
do a day's work?

09:27.280 --> 09:28.840
[Arthur] In the old days, Finn,

09:29.720 --> 09:33.480
family meetings
used to be all of us together.

09:33.560 --> 09:35.000
[Polly] Arthur, shut up.

09:39.640 --> 09:41.080
Now, me and John,

09:43.080 --> 09:49.240
we're just fucking bin men
whose duty it is to obey.

09:50.680 --> 09:51.680
Hmm?

09:55.920 --> 09:57.320
Mrs. Changretta.

10:00.720 --> 10:07.280
Arthur, shut up.
Finn, go and get us cigars.

10:07.400 --> 10:11.200
[John] So what are we gonna do
all night, eh? Climb fucking trees?

10:11.280 --> 10:12.920
John, stop swearing in front of the kids.

10:13.000 --> 10:14.640
Yeah, and who said
you're staying the night?

10:14.720 --> 10:16.120
[Arthur] I know what we can do.

10:17.000 --> 10:18.560
We get the guns out, John.

10:19.240 --> 10:22.560
We go outside,
and we shoot some fucking pheasants.

10:23.040 --> 10:24.120
[both laugh]

10:24.720 --> 10:26.600
-That's what the bosses do, isn't it?
-Yeah.

10:26.680 --> 10:27.880
Fuck off, Arthur.

10:30.440 --> 10:31.960
Fuck you just say to me?

10:34.000 --> 10:36.400
I didn't ask for separate meetings today,
all right?

10:36.800 --> 10:41.120
No. No, what the fuck did you just say?

10:41.480 --> 10:43.960
'Cause I didn't fucking hear you right.

10:45.320 --> 10:50.040
I didn't ask for separate meetings today,
all right?

10:50.480 --> 10:51.560
Fucking pheasant.

10:52.240 --> 10:53.520
-Carl!
-[laughs]

10:53.960 --> 10:55.520
You can't say things like that.

10:55.600 --> 10:56.600
Now look what you've done.

11:00.160 --> 11:01.600
All right, brothers.

11:02.800 --> 11:04.400
It's just the fucking whiskey talking.

11:04.480 --> 11:06.400
I don't ask to be protected, all right?

11:06.480 --> 11:10.040
[Polly] Right. Shut up.
The pair of you, sit down!

11:12.040 --> 11:13.360
Sit down!

11:13.640 --> 11:15.520
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Look around you.

11:16.680 --> 11:18.080
And look at this house.

11:19.400 --> 11:20.960
Look where we are.

11:21.040 --> 11:23.320
Look how far we've come.

11:23.400 --> 11:25.480
I think it's about time
we all started acting

11:25.560 --> 11:27.760
in a way more appropriate to our station.

11:30.120 --> 11:32.240
We're none of us bin men anymore, Arthur.

11:33.960 --> 11:35.520
Tommy needs us all together.

11:37.320 --> 11:39.120
I'd like to propose a toast.

11:41.680 --> 11:42.680
[clears throat]

11:47.560 --> 11:51.120
It's a family united
that shall never be defeated.

11:51.360 --> 11:53.200
-[door opens]
-[footsteps approaching]

11:53.560 --> 11:56.960
Tommy's gone. Swear to God,
he's in a wagon with Johnny Dogs.

11:59.760 --> 12:00.760
Shit.

12:01.160 --> 12:02.680
This is what he does now.

12:10.880 --> 12:14.160
-[Arthur] Tommy! Wait!
-[Polly] Arthur!

12:14.240 --> 12:15.880
-[Arthur] Tommy!
-[Polly] Arthur, let him go!

12:16.160 --> 12:19.520
-[Arthur] Tommy! Tommy!
-[John] Tommy! Tommy!

12:21.360 --> 12:22.600
Tommy!

12:25.440 --> 12:26.720
Walk on. Walk on.

12:28.840 --> 12:30.400
-[Dogs] Tommy.
-[Tommy] Walk on.

12:31.160 --> 12:32.760
They're coming out in the drive.

12:33.360 --> 12:35.240
-You're not gonna tell them?
-Tell them what?

12:36.040 --> 12:37.440
That we're going to Wales.

12:38.040 --> 12:39.040
I left a note.

12:41.560 --> 12:42.840
Did you tell them
why we're going to Wales?

12:42.920 --> 12:43.960
No.

12:44.040 --> 12:46.160
At some point you're gonna tell me
why we're going to Wales?

12:46.240 --> 12:47.640
Yeah, when we get there.

12:48.440 --> 12:49.480
[Tommy] Walk on.

12:49.560 --> 12:51.360
Should have brought
at least one woman, Tommy.

12:51.440 --> 12:53.520
Johnny, it's a woman we're going to see.

12:54.280 --> 12:56.920
-There, boy. Walk on. Walk on.
-Right.

13:01.080 --> 13:03.680
Says he'll be back in Birmingham
in three days.

13:05.120 --> 13:06.400
[Polly sighs] Let him go.

13:07.120 --> 13:10.240
The important thing is,
if he says he'll be back, he'll be back.

13:10.960 --> 13:14.040
Come on.
Let's go light a fire in the big room.

13:14.560 --> 13:18.120
Let's go drink whiskey, with water.

13:28.960 --> 13:30.400
See to the horses, Johnny.

13:30.720 --> 13:32.040
Aye, Tom.

13:38.640 --> 13:39.680
[sighs]

13:47.280 --> 13:51.200
So we'll go out through Meridian,
then into the Black Mountains.

13:53.800 --> 13:55.440
-Here.
-[yells]

13:55.520 --> 13:56.920
Here, give me some.

13:57.840 --> 13:58.880
Boy.

14:01.200 --> 14:02.280
Here you go.

14:06.560 --> 14:09.960
Now, remember last night
when you asked after Mama?

14:12.200 --> 14:15.080
She's gone, Charlie, and there's
a few things we need to get straight.

14:16.960 --> 14:18.320
There's her photographs.

14:19.400 --> 14:20.880
There's her clothes.

14:24.040 --> 14:25.960
I'll keep things the way they are
in the room. [clears throat]

14:28.880 --> 14:32.800
Just keep things the way they are.

14:38.240 --> 14:39.280
Here you go.

14:41.320 --> 14:43.440
Yeah. Here you go.

14:45.360 --> 14:46.840
I'm not much good, Charlie.

14:48.120 --> 14:50.440
-[Charlie exclaims]
-You'll find that out soon enough.

14:53.760 --> 14:56.120
She's not gonna be coming back,
so it's just you and me.

14:59.440 --> 15:03.560
She'll be with us in our hearts
'cause we love her.

15:04.160 --> 15:05.200
-[Dogs] Tommy.
-Yeah.

15:05.280 --> 15:07.080
This fucking horse of yours
won't come to me.

15:07.160 --> 15:09.080
-All right, I'll be there. All right.
-Huh? Come on.

15:11.120 --> 15:12.920
That was her favorite horse, Charlie,

15:14.640 --> 15:16.680
and he's been all over the place
since she's gone.

15:18.760 --> 15:20.320
-Tom?
-Yeah, you watch him.

15:20.400 --> 15:21.600
I will. Oh, yeah.

15:22.480 --> 15:23.480
Huh?

15:34.320 --> 15:37.480
All right, now cock it with your thumb.

15:41.000 --> 15:42.560
-[chuckles]
-[gun cocks]

15:44.960 --> 15:48.080
There you go. Now she's been cocked.

15:48.440 --> 15:50.320
-She's alive in your hand.
-[crowing]

15:50.800 --> 15:53.320
It's like waking up a girl
when you cock that trigger.

15:54.080 --> 15:57.400
She rolls over all sleepy-eyed
and she goes,

15:58.080 --> 16:01.640
-"Michael. Michael."
-[John chuckling]

16:02.760 --> 16:04.840
"What are you gonna make me do, Michael?"

16:04.920 --> 16:08.680
You boys are fucking crazy men.

16:08.760 --> 16:11.720
-Yeah, but you feel it, though, right?
-Yeah.

16:12.120 --> 16:13.320
You feel it.

16:13.400 --> 16:15.760
Yeah, you can feel the power.

16:16.280 --> 16:19.280
Now, squeeze it.

16:22.120 --> 16:23.120
[gunshot]

16:24.800 --> 16:25.960
Powerful.

16:26.040 --> 16:29.400
-Fucking useless.
-Piss off, John.

16:29.480 --> 16:36.120
Michael, why does a pen pusher who sits
on his ass all day wanna fire a gun?

16:36.400 --> 16:38.520
Hmm? Eh?

16:39.520 --> 16:41.080
Cock it again.

16:42.440 --> 16:44.080
-Cock it again.
-[John] Cock it again.

16:44.240 --> 16:45.440
Round two.

16:47.800 --> 16:49.320
-[gun cocks]
-[Arthur] Mmm.

16:50.240 --> 16:52.480
Look at that fucking face, John boy.

16:53.480 --> 16:55.080
Look at that face.

16:56.240 --> 16:57.880
Now he feels it.

16:58.560 --> 17:00.840
But you won't feel nothing

17:01.520 --> 17:05.680
until you point that thing on a man.

17:07.720 --> 17:10.640
So do it.

17:17.720 --> 17:20.440
There you go, young boss.

17:21.880 --> 17:24.720
There you go. Now you feel it.

17:24.800 --> 17:27.040
Now you feel what we feel.

17:27.920 --> 17:30.520
This is what it's like.

17:31.520 --> 17:35.040
Michael, that's a Webley.

17:35.640 --> 17:37.160
Jumps on the hammer.

17:37.760 --> 17:39.600
How does it feel, Michael, huh?

17:40.920 --> 17:43.240
Better than having a pen
in your hand, isn't it?

17:44.080 --> 17:48.160
More like having your cock in your hand.
Yeah.

17:48.760 --> 17:50.040
Yeah, it is.

17:52.640 --> 17:54.520
One squeeze.

17:55.480 --> 17:56.480
[grunts]

17:57.320 --> 17:58.320
I'm gone.

17:59.440 --> 18:01.200
I'm fucking mate.

18:01.600 --> 18:05.600
Michael, you fucking watch
that Webley don't jump. You know that?

18:05.880 --> 18:08.280
When you pull that fucking trigger,

18:09.600 --> 18:13.960
and the body of the man you shot
wraps itself around your ankles,

18:15.720 --> 18:18.640
-they pile up.
-[Michael breathing heavily]

18:19.360 --> 18:22.800
It gets to the point
where you can't walk in a room

18:24.080 --> 18:26.440
without bringing a load of them with you.

18:31.000 --> 18:32.440
[Polly] What's going on?

18:40.680 --> 18:41.680
What's going on?

18:41.960 --> 18:46.400
Polly, we're just educating the boss here

18:47.640 --> 18:49.400
on our side of the business.

18:51.640 --> 18:55.200
Michael, get in the house.

19:12.480 --> 19:15.360
I'm not a fucking kid anymore.

19:36.760 --> 19:39.240
[gunshots]

19:47.160 --> 19:49.200
[gunshots]

20:41.960 --> 20:43.200
You've come to tell me it's canceled.

20:43.280 --> 20:44.720
No, why would it be?

20:44.800 --> 20:45.880
I read the papers.

20:45.960 --> 20:48.400
-This is business.
-It won't work.

20:49.360 --> 20:51.480
I told your brother,
this whole fucking plan won't work.

20:51.560 --> 20:53.800
If Tommy wants to keep this secret...
Tell him.

20:53.880 --> 20:57.080
There was a woman in a fur coat
walking through here in broad daylight

20:57.160 --> 21:00.280
like the Queen of fucking Sheba
asking about armored cars.

21:00.360 --> 21:04.040
During a period of grieving,
some things were allowed to slip.

21:04.560 --> 21:07.440
We know the woman. We're dealing with it.

21:08.080 --> 21:11.440
Now, take a look at this list.

21:11.520 --> 21:13.360
These are all the men
who work the night shift

21:13.440 --> 21:16.120
who are members
of the South Birmingham Communist Party.

21:16.200 --> 21:19.760
You've got six weeks. Sack them all.

21:30.440 --> 21:32.000
Are you fucking mad?

21:32.880 --> 21:34.040
He is.

21:35.000 --> 21:36.000
Yeah.

21:36.320 --> 21:38.160
Every factory in the city
will come out on strike.

21:38.240 --> 21:41.520
So? You find reasons.

21:43.120 --> 21:44.480
You set them up.

21:45.800 --> 21:47.000
You sack them.

21:47.080 --> 21:48.240
Look at the list again.

21:48.880 --> 21:51.400
Are there any communists on your shift
who aren't on the list?

21:54.440 --> 21:55.560
No.

21:56.680 --> 21:58.680
Please don't fucking lie to us.

21:58.760 --> 22:00.960
-Who's missing?
-I don't know.

22:05.560 --> 22:06.680
Emmanuel Hunter.

22:07.960 --> 22:08.960
Hmm?

22:10.840 --> 22:16.040
Convener, deputy treasurer,
Sparkhill Communist Party.

22:16.720 --> 22:18.560
They've operated here.

22:19.440 --> 22:20.760
I didn't know he was a communist.

22:21.400 --> 22:24.000
We left that name off the list on purpose.

22:25.280 --> 22:27.360
See if you could be trusted.

22:29.000 --> 22:30.440
You can't be trusted.

22:30.520 --> 22:32.640
Look, I'm just a working man.

22:32.720 --> 22:34.280
[John] We're gonna be watching you.

22:35.560 --> 22:38.280
-Watching your fucking house.
-I've got kids.

22:41.160 --> 22:42.280
Ethan and John.

22:46.720 --> 22:48.280
Just get them sacked

22:49.920 --> 22:52.560
as they appear on the list, two a week.

22:53.800 --> 22:56.440
The last one before the clocks go forward.

22:58.440 --> 23:00.080
Is that a yes or a no?

23:02.120 --> 23:03.560
-Yes.
-Thank you.

23:07.000 --> 23:09.560
-[metal clanking]
-[men shouting indistinctly]

23:20.560 --> 23:21.680
Good?

23:22.480 --> 23:23.560
Good.

23:36.400 --> 23:38.680
-Do you think he'll return?
-Tommy?

23:43.440 --> 23:44.760
He'll always come back.

23:46.880 --> 23:47.880
You speak differently when you talk--

23:47.960 --> 23:49.720
I prefer to talk about other things.

23:50.440 --> 23:51.680
Let me see.

23:53.280 --> 23:56.160
What books do you like?

23:57.320 --> 24:00.280
Riding, flower arranging, embroidery?

24:00.360 --> 24:02.360
You'd be surprised of the things I know.

24:05.760 --> 24:08.080
You'd also be surprised
of the things I don't know.

24:09.200 --> 24:11.280
What could you possibly not know?

24:12.520 --> 24:13.880
I wasn't educated

24:19.920 --> 24:22.240
-at all.
-What is there to learn, after all?

24:31.080 --> 24:32.080
Goodness.

24:34.320 --> 24:36.600
I'm sorry. You must need a rest.

24:48.960 --> 24:51.200
Do you tell your friends
you're painting a gangster?

24:54.560 --> 24:56.120
Is that the fun in all of this?

24:57.040 --> 24:58.600
In truth, I don't have any friends.

25:00.360 --> 25:02.080
I knew everyone through my wife.

25:04.640 --> 25:05.920
When she died,

25:09.760 --> 25:10.840
well...

25:14.640 --> 25:15.880
Look, Polly,

25:17.920 --> 25:20.320
my motivation for doing this is twofold.

25:21.280 --> 25:26.040
Firstly, you have a face
full of contradictions,

25:27.200 --> 25:29.800
and it's a challenge
to capture them in one expression.

25:30.120 --> 25:32.000
-[scoffs]
-That's the sales pitch.

25:33.960 --> 25:39.720
The second motivation is that
I am planning to seduce you eventually

25:41.240 --> 25:43.200
and, please God, sleep with you.

25:43.640 --> 25:45.240
How would that please God?

25:45.880 --> 25:47.280
Please me.

26:24.920 --> 26:26.080
And stop.

26:31.440 --> 26:32.920
And he didn't say what he wants.

26:34.000 --> 26:35.800
When he was drunk, he said absolution.

26:36.440 --> 26:37.800
Other than that, nothing.

26:58.360 --> 27:00.360
Thank you for your time, Madame Boswell.

27:02.040 --> 27:03.920
I heard someone shot your wife.

27:09.000 --> 27:11.600
If you're looking for soldiers,
our men are all up at Appleby.

27:11.800 --> 27:13.560
I have no need for soldiers.

27:14.640 --> 27:16.080
It's not why I came here.

27:28.480 --> 27:29.480
What do you think?

27:29.800 --> 27:31.040
You're selling?

27:31.120 --> 27:32.280
Giving.

27:34.000 --> 27:35.640
-Why?
-Would you take it?

27:37.560 --> 27:38.760
I'd take it.

27:39.480 --> 27:40.680
Would you wear it?

27:40.760 --> 27:42.760
-Why would I not?
-That's my question.

27:50.440 --> 27:52.800
My wife was wearing it
the night she was shot,

27:55.800 --> 28:01.320
and I lie awake at night
at 4:00 in the fucking morning,

28:01.400 --> 28:03.800
and I blame myself for her death.

28:05.640 --> 28:07.400
I pushed some people too far.

28:09.160 --> 28:11.760
You want me to tell you
this jewel is cursed,

28:14.320 --> 28:16.600
and then her death won't be
all your fault.

28:24.440 --> 28:26.520
If I believed in the priests,

28:27.280 --> 28:29.520
I would confess and ask for forgiveness,

28:30.840 --> 28:33.760
but all I have is you, Madame Boswell.

28:35.280 --> 28:36.760
I have a son.

28:38.920 --> 28:40.680
I have a business.

28:41.240 --> 28:42.800
I need to get some sleep.

28:46.600 --> 28:47.960
It is cursed.

28:50.160 --> 28:53.440
I feel its curse burning through my heart.

29:00.360 --> 29:02.280
Bless you, Tommy Shelby.

29:03.280 --> 29:05.400
You'll have good fortune from now on.

29:05.480 --> 29:07.920
-The business is done?
-It's done.

29:08.960 --> 29:11.720
You're not going to give me
one fucking clue what that was about?

29:12.360 --> 29:15.840
All religion is a foolish answer
to a foolish question.

29:16.200 --> 29:17.440
What does that mean?

29:17.520 --> 29:18.920
Go and get Charlie from the camp.

29:19.000 --> 29:21.000
He'll have learned enough
bad habits by now.

29:22.000 --> 29:23.920
You can drop us to the train station.

29:24.920 --> 29:28.400
And Johnny boy, if I were you,

29:28.640 --> 29:31.880
I'd come back here tonight later on.

29:34.280 --> 29:36.680
It's gonna be
one hell of a big fucking party.

29:41.520 --> 29:44.360
[man] The day and date on your ticket.

29:44.480 --> 29:47.920
If you can't read, find someone who can.

29:48.760 --> 29:52.440
Tickets for sailings other than today's
will be destroyed.

29:52.560 --> 29:56.400
He has people all over the docks. If it's
going to happen, it will happen now.

29:56.480 --> 29:58.000
We'll be all right.

29:58.080 --> 30:01.280
Why don't these Irish
fill in their papers in advance?

30:01.360 --> 30:05.320
Think about Mott Street, the café,
the smell of the coffee.

30:05.400 --> 30:06.400
[speaking Italian]

30:53.000 --> 30:56.080
Police! Help! Police!

30:59.000 --> 31:02.200
Officer, there are some men,
they mean us harm.

31:02.280 --> 31:05.680
We are in danger here.
Can you escort us to the dock?

31:07.640 --> 31:08.680
Please.

31:08.840 --> 31:10.000
Come with me.

31:11.640 --> 31:14.200
Excuse me, brother. You got a light?

32:03.160 --> 32:04.200
Thank you, Officer.

32:05.360 --> 32:07.280
-That'll be all.
-John Shelby.

32:08.560 --> 32:13.760
Is that the lad I used to teach?
John Shelby, I smacked your ass.

32:14.360 --> 32:15.480
Let him go.

32:16.600 --> 32:19.320
-Please. Please, let her go.
-Arthur?

32:19.840 --> 32:23.880
How many times I looked the other way
because of your sweet smile.

32:24.360 --> 32:26.920
I said, let him go. He's coming with us.

32:28.080 --> 32:30.640
Not until I know my wife is safe.

32:31.600 --> 32:34.600
She's safe. We're not going to harm her.

32:35.400 --> 32:36.400
Let's just get a move on.

32:36.480 --> 32:40.320
Look, we're disobeying somebody's orders
just by talking to you.

32:41.600 --> 32:43.800
Don't push it, please.

32:45.400 --> 32:47.520
-Come with us. Let him go.
-[Audrey] Let him go, too.

32:47.840 --> 32:49.280
Say it's done.

32:49.960 --> 32:53.120
Say he's in the harbor.
He can do you no harm from New York.

32:53.200 --> 32:57.320
I can't do that, Mrs. Changretta.
I can't do that. Sorry.

32:57.400 --> 32:59.360
Okay, okay. Audrey, listen.

32:59.440 --> 33:01.000
-No!
-Listen to me!

33:01.800 --> 33:05.680
Go to the café in Mott Street.
Bonito will take care of you.

33:05.880 --> 33:09.320
Let him go, too. He's an old man.

33:09.640 --> 33:11.520
I gave you sweets and cakes.

33:11.600 --> 33:13.160
Mrs. Changretta, there are rules.

33:14.000 --> 33:15.680
Your husband knows the rules.

33:16.960 --> 33:18.280
-Come on, old man.
-[Audrey] No.

33:20.480 --> 33:21.720
Sorry.

33:23.560 --> 33:25.520
We're disobeying orders here.

33:26.280 --> 33:29.320
Let him fucking go!

33:30.800 --> 33:33.480
You have 10 seconds,
or Tommy's orders stand.

33:34.560 --> 33:36.600
They stand. One!

33:37.880 --> 33:39.840
-Two!
-Please!

33:41.680 --> 33:43.000
Three.

33:47.000 --> 33:49.000
-I love you forever.
-Four.

33:52.840 --> 33:54.120
[sobbing]

34:00.040 --> 34:05.600
-No, no, no!
-America. A new life.

34:05.680 --> 34:09.240
No, no, no! [wailing]

34:09.320 --> 34:10.720
A new love.

34:16.400 --> 34:18.560
[continues wailing]

35:27.920 --> 35:29.960
[praying in Italian]

35:43.280 --> 35:46.320
Do you know what time it is, old man?

35:49.320 --> 35:50.920
I'll tell you.

35:51.440 --> 35:53.400
[continues praying]

35:55.520 --> 35:57.280
It's after 7:00 in the evening,

36:00.000 --> 36:04.760
and I'm going to keep you alive
until it gets light.

36:10.360 --> 36:13.040
I'll not deliver the final cut

36:13.880 --> 36:16.840
until we can both hear
the blackbirds singing outside.

36:23.360 --> 36:25.640
It's a beautiful sound,

36:28.320 --> 36:30.320
which my wife will never hear again.

36:45.160 --> 36:48.440
Now, I'm gonna have to choose carefully

36:50.920 --> 36:54.240
which part of you I cut away first.

36:58.440 --> 36:59.840
Open your eyes.

37:00.840 --> 37:05.560
Open your eyes,
or I will cut away your fucking eyelids!

37:09.360 --> 37:11.080
Now look at me.

37:12.200 --> 37:13.880
Look at me.

37:15.840 --> 37:17.320
This is the end.

37:19.360 --> 37:20.880
This is the end.

37:27.880 --> 37:30.160
It was your tongue that gave the order.

37:33.720 --> 37:36.040
I'll take your tongue first.

37:38.760 --> 37:40.520
Then I'll take your ears.

37:43.080 --> 37:45.280
Then I'll take your fingers.

37:46.560 --> 37:48.480
Then your fucking toes.

37:49.880 --> 37:54.280
See, I take your balls first,
you drain too fast like you fuckers do.

37:57.080 --> 38:01.280
No, I think tongue first. Tongue first.

38:01.600 --> 38:03.240
[muffled groaning]

38:04.920 --> 38:05.920
Tongue first.

38:09.600 --> 38:11.680
[breathing heavily]

38:12.520 --> 38:16.400
If I take your tongue,
you won't be able to explain,

38:17.480 --> 38:21.960
and I want you to explain.
I want you to fucking explain.

38:35.240 --> 38:37.440
[Tommy breathing heavily]

38:41.920 --> 38:43.960
[continues praying]

38:54.680 --> 38:55.840
Come on, Tommy.

38:58.720 --> 39:00.720
I forget who I am.

39:01.640 --> 39:03.120
I forget who I am.

39:04.240 --> 39:07.040
I'm a Blinder.
I'll take your fucking eyes first!

39:07.280 --> 39:08.280
[gunshot]

39:13.680 --> 39:15.760
I heard the blackbird sing.

39:29.280 --> 39:32.360
And we let his wife
board the immigrant ship to New York.

39:33.240 --> 39:35.520
We didn't kill Mrs. Changretta.

39:37.120 --> 39:38.400
It's all right.

39:42.320 --> 39:44.520
We're not those kind of men.

40:12.760 --> 40:13.760
[sighs]

40:14.720 --> 40:16.520
You get rid of the body, John.

40:18.480 --> 40:22.240
Get rid of those for good.

41:09.000 --> 41:10.640
All gone.

41:10.840 --> 41:11.840
[exclaims]

41:14.400 --> 41:15.400
Oh!

41:51.960 --> 41:52.960
[sighs]

42:01.200 --> 42:03.520
Did you do what was on your list, Ada?

42:03.600 --> 42:05.600
You and your fucking lists.

42:06.360 --> 42:07.680
Did you?

42:10.080 --> 42:12.680
I spoke to an old friend of Freddie's.

42:12.760 --> 42:15.480
He's a Communist Party candidate
for Basall Heath.

42:15.560 --> 42:19.360
I asked him about the Birmingham branch
of the National Vigilance Committee.

42:20.880 --> 42:24.840
He said he'd heard the Soviet Embassy
was getting information from the inside.

42:25.480 --> 42:27.760
And? Has he got a name?

42:29.440 --> 42:30.560
Yes.

42:32.920 --> 42:34.880
But just promise me
no one will get killed.

42:35.040 --> 42:39.560
Ada, it'll be me or John or Arthur
who gets killed

42:39.640 --> 42:41.200
if you don't give me the fucking name.

42:42.360 --> 42:45.240
There's someone ahead of us,
and I need to know why.

42:47.440 --> 42:48.920
James Monkland.

42:49.800 --> 42:53.000
He's a Lloyds underwriter.
He's got an office on Curzon Street.

42:53.120 --> 42:55.320
Tommy, for fuck's sake,
who is it that's ahead of you?

42:56.720 --> 42:57.880
I knew I could count on you, Ada.

42:58.080 --> 43:01.240
No, you can't,
and I just asked you a fucking question.

43:06.080 --> 43:09.200
And I notice
you started wearing lipstick again.

43:09.960 --> 43:10.960
[scoffs]

43:11.680 --> 43:13.040
So what?

43:16.840 --> 43:18.120
I got bored.

43:18.200 --> 43:22.240
You can change what you do,
but you can't change what you want.

43:24.120 --> 43:25.320
And what is it that I want?

43:32.800 --> 43:38.440
There's gonna be a vacancy coming up
at Shelby Company Limited.

43:41.840 --> 43:43.440
Boston office.

43:43.800 --> 43:45.240
Boston, America?

43:46.960 --> 43:50.080
Lipstick. Gloves from Paris.

43:51.360 --> 43:53.240
No revolvers. All legal.

43:54.280 --> 43:57.400
Just turn a few heads.
Do the transit deals.

44:07.280 --> 44:08.880
James Monkland, right?

44:12.400 --> 44:14.360
Good night. I love you.

44:26.880 --> 44:29.440
-James Monkland?
-Yours, sir.

44:54.920 --> 44:56.160
Who the hell are you?

44:57.920 --> 44:59.000
What do you want with me?

44:59.080 --> 45:01.240
You've been passing information
about a robbery

45:01.320 --> 45:03.320
at the Lanchester factory in Sparkbrook.

45:05.000 --> 45:08.680
Are you Tommy Shelby?

45:08.760 --> 45:11.720
I need to know the name of the person
in the organization

45:11.800 --> 45:13.000
that was giving you information.

45:16.040 --> 45:17.200
What organization?

45:18.840 --> 45:20.920
The Economic League,
the Vigilance Committee,

45:21.000 --> 45:22.760
the Odd Fellows, Section D.

45:23.440 --> 45:25.200
They have many fucking names.

45:25.280 --> 45:26.520
Shit, shit, shit.

45:27.320 --> 45:29.400
Give me the name of the informant.

45:36.000 --> 45:37.560
Mr. Shelby,

45:40.040 --> 45:42.200
they are very, very dangerous people.

45:42.280 --> 45:44.240
Oh. Hmm.

45:47.080 --> 45:50.520
Well, unfortunately, so are we.

45:52.440 --> 45:54.400
You have to choose
who you're more afraid of.

45:54.800 --> 45:57.360
The Peaky Blinders at exactly 11:43,

45:57.440 --> 46:02.480
or Section D at some point in the future.

46:06.200 --> 46:08.880
If you make the wrong choice,
you won't see 11:44.

46:11.080 --> 46:14.000
[Linda] Do they always have to do
the stock taking at night, Arthur?

46:14.080 --> 46:17.360
[Arthur] Only 'cause, you know,
it slows down production.

46:18.280 --> 46:19.560
Thank you.

46:22.760 --> 46:23.920
Thank you.

46:37.560 --> 46:39.360
Night work will have to end.

46:39.520 --> 46:41.120
It will. It will.

46:41.920 --> 46:44.320
You'll have things to do at night.

46:50.360 --> 46:51.360
Yeah.

46:52.800 --> 46:57.400
You and I, we've spoken about it.

46:57.920 --> 47:00.720
I was gonna wait until you had
a strong cup of tea in your hand.

47:00.800 --> 47:04.120
-Come on, then.
-But I'm gonna have a baby, Arthur.

47:19.560 --> 47:20.560
Pregnant?

47:21.680 --> 47:23.040
Yeah.

47:25.960 --> 47:29.720
You said you spent the night taking stock.
Well, so did I.

47:30.840 --> 47:33.600
This working at night will have to stop.

47:41.840 --> 47:43.880
-You'll have a baby.
-Yes.

47:45.800 --> 47:46.800
[chuckles]

47:55.640 --> 47:57.320
-Oh, it's great news.
-[chuckles]

47:58.120 --> 47:59.120
[exhales]

48:02.120 --> 48:03.520
Right, then.

48:04.000 --> 48:05.520
[chuckles]

48:05.600 --> 48:08.800
Let's have a cup of tea. One moment.

48:16.160 --> 48:17.160
[laughs]

48:17.680 --> 48:19.920
Hop off. Let's have that tea.

48:26.800 --> 48:28.320
Arthur, for fuck's sake, what is it?

48:28.400 --> 48:31.600
No. We wait for Tommy.

48:33.320 --> 48:35.000
I've got a stolen statue back there

48:35.080 --> 48:37.280
with its dick hanging out
waiting to be melted down.

48:38.160 --> 48:39.720
Tell us. Tell Tommy later.

48:39.800 --> 48:42.440
Yeah, look, he's not here.
He's not here. I'm going.

48:43.200 --> 48:44.240
-Hold your horses.
-There he is.

48:44.320 --> 48:45.680
-Bye, Curly.
-There he is.

48:45.760 --> 48:47.000
All right, what is it?

48:47.080 --> 48:49.920
-Arthur's fucking giving us all this shit.
-Come on. Come on.

48:50.040 --> 48:51.320
Right.

48:54.160 --> 48:56.440
Arthur you got wire on the fucking cork.
Give it here.

48:56.520 --> 48:59.440
Bastard. Right. Gentlemen!

49:06.040 --> 49:11.520
Linda is up the swanny.
I'm gonna be a fucking dad.

49:12.040 --> 49:14.320
-Fuck off. [chuckles]
-[all laughing]

49:14.920 --> 49:17.200
Yes, Curly. Yeah.

49:18.200 --> 49:21.080
Arthur, I knew you had it in you.

49:21.600 --> 49:23.120
I knew he had it in him.

49:23.200 --> 49:24.400
September she reckons.

49:25.160 --> 49:26.680
Her tits feel different already.

49:26.760 --> 49:28.960
Yeah, that's not the only thing
that's gonna be different, brother.

49:29.160 --> 49:30.920
You're fucked now, man.

49:31.200 --> 49:32.880
Fucked. Absolutely fucked.

49:33.040 --> 49:35.200
Oh, nothing's gonna change, John.

49:36.720 --> 49:37.800
Goodbye, Arthur.

49:39.880 --> 49:43.040
-I have a meeting I have to go to.
-Yeah.

49:43.760 --> 49:45.400
Yeah, of course you do.

49:49.400 --> 49:50.520
Yeah, you...

49:52.520 --> 49:53.760
You go to your meeting.

49:55.000 --> 49:56.600
Congratulations.

49:57.320 --> 49:59.360
-I'm gonna be a dad.
-Proud of you.

50:24.120 --> 50:26.600
[violin playing]

50:36.800 --> 50:37.800
[door opens]

50:38.240 --> 50:40.080
Your Highness, Mr. Thomas Shelby.

50:44.840 --> 50:46.640
Welcome, Mr. Shelby.

50:46.720 --> 50:51.040
I believe you've met everyone
apart from my wife,

50:51.920 --> 50:54.040
Grand Duchess Izabella Petrovna.

50:55.920 --> 50:57.400
Please, take a seat.

51:02.960 --> 51:05.080
Before we begin, Mr. Shelby,

51:05.360 --> 51:08.360
we must offer you our sincere condolences
on your recent loss,

51:09.600 --> 51:11.120
which some of us witnessed.

51:12.480 --> 51:13.480
[Tommy sniffles]

51:16.200 --> 51:18.800
-Did you drive, Mr. Shelby?
-Yes.

51:24.160 --> 51:27.120
-They say you're an expert on cars.
-Yes, I am.

51:27.200 --> 51:30.480
I am curious.
What was your father's profession?

51:30.600 --> 51:33.760
Well, he told fortunes,
and he stole horses.

51:33.840 --> 51:37.080
Often, he would tell a man
that his horse would be stolen,

51:37.160 --> 51:39.680
and they would marvel at his powers
when it was.

51:45.960 --> 51:48.560
Before we eat, should we say grace?

51:53.360 --> 51:58.600
For what we are about to receive,
may the Lord make us truly thankful.

51:59.960 --> 52:01.840
-Amen.
-I'm not here to eat.

52:02.760 --> 52:04.160
I'm here to do business.

52:04.600 --> 52:07.240
What I have to say can be said
before the main course.

52:07.320 --> 52:09.000
Then I will leave you all to your evening.

52:09.400 --> 52:14.880
Grand Duchess, I must apologize
for the bad manners of my compatriot.

52:15.040 --> 52:18.200
This is a report on the mission's progress
so far. [clears throat]

52:18.440 --> 52:20.680
I've made only one copy for security.

52:22.240 --> 52:23.440
Who should I give it to?

52:23.520 --> 52:26.120
My husband is in charge of this operation.

52:27.480 --> 52:31.480
But since there will no doubt
be vodka later,

52:31.560 --> 52:34.080
perhaps you should give it to me
for safe-keeping.

52:37.440 --> 52:40.000
Speak, Mr. Shelby, while we eat.

52:44.320 --> 52:47.800
Five factory foremen on our payroll
have begun a campaign of victimization

52:47.880 --> 52:50.520
against communist workers
in five factories across Birmingham.

52:52.240 --> 52:55.040
Anger amongst the workers will grow,
but we will control it.

52:55.120 --> 52:57.040
On the night of June 21st,

52:57.240 --> 52:59.800
a general strike will be called
across the city.

53:00.280 --> 53:03.760
Protests will develop into riots,

53:03.840 --> 53:07.320
and all police that are not
already under our control will be busy.

53:07.560 --> 53:09.040
The city will be paralyzed.

53:09.640 --> 53:11.360
So how will you move the train?

53:11.440 --> 53:13.360
We have two locomotive drivers

53:13.440 --> 53:16.400
who've been allocated to drive
the midnight goods train to London.

53:16.480 --> 53:18.760
The armored vehicles will be waiting
on flatbeds.

53:18.840 --> 53:20.720
-And ammunition?
-The ammunition--

53:20.800 --> 53:23.880
I have to say
that this soup is exceptional.

53:27.360 --> 53:28.920
Absolutely delicious.

53:29.880 --> 53:33.680
Ammunition, incendiaries will already
have been packed up and crated

53:33.760 --> 53:35.280
for transport to Istanbul.

53:35.360 --> 53:38.480
-And how long to London?
-The train won't reach London.

53:39.000 --> 53:42.640
All the goods will be unloaded
at a coal yard at St. Albans

53:43.120 --> 53:44.880
and put onto Shelby Company trucks.

53:44.960 --> 53:46.840
From there, they will go directly
to the Poplar Docks.

53:46.920 --> 53:50.360
You Highness, if you're having difficulty
understanding his accent,

53:50.440 --> 53:53.800
then I can go through the plan with you
at a later date.

53:54.000 --> 53:55.840
If there is no ship waiting for my men,

53:55.920 --> 53:59.680
all goods will be dumped into the sea
before first light.

53:59.760 --> 54:02.120
What happens when they discover
the armored cars are missing?

54:02.200 --> 54:06.360
During the rioting,
the Lanchester factory will be firebombed.

54:06.440 --> 54:08.960
A scrap metal dealer of my acquaintance
will declare

54:09.040 --> 54:11.200
that all the armored vehicles
are in the wreckage

54:11.280 --> 54:13.040
and should be written off as salvage.

54:13.120 --> 54:15.320
No one will know
that they are in your possession.

54:15.760 --> 54:19.040
We formulated this plan
when we met at Birmingham.

54:20.360 --> 54:22.640
I'm certain that
nothing has been overlooked.

54:25.560 --> 54:31.880
This is the amount of extra expense
I believe I will incur

54:31.960 --> 54:33.720
for trucks and fuels.

54:34.520 --> 54:36.440
I trust you will respond in kind.

54:38.280 --> 54:39.960
But of course, Mr. Shelby.

54:43.640 --> 54:44.960
Before I go,

54:46.160 --> 54:50.600
I would like it known
that I'm unable to swallow food

54:51.320 --> 54:53.040
in the same room as this priest.

54:57.400 --> 54:58.760
Enjoy your evening.

55:07.960 --> 55:11.040
Tatiana, see Mr. Shelby to his car.

55:11.120 --> 55:12.520
Yes.

55:19.800 --> 55:20.800
[speaking Russian]

55:40.440 --> 55:41.640
Walk with me.

56:05.040 --> 56:07.440
The priest is passing information
about the robbery

56:07.520 --> 56:09.200
to a Lloyds underwriter called Monkland.

56:09.280 --> 56:12.880
He, in turn, is passing information
to the Soviet Embassy.

56:13.600 --> 56:15.920
You want him dead?
I'll kill him, no charge.

56:17.520 --> 56:19.760
Why would the priest
pass information to our enemies?

56:26.000 --> 56:30.480
I'm being paid to act and to observe,
like a soldier.

56:30.800 --> 56:33.520
The complexities are your business.

56:33.880 --> 56:36.320
Go and speak to Izabella.
I trust her to decide.

56:40.920 --> 56:44.360
You were able to contain your business
dealings even after what happened.

56:46.320 --> 56:47.640
Perhaps you didn't love her.

56:55.520 --> 56:59.400
She's here by my side,

57:01.000 --> 57:03.920
and she says, "Don't trust these people."

57:08.520 --> 57:12.240
Now give me permission to kill the priest.

57:36.720 --> 57:39.000
♪ On a gathering storm comes ♪

57:39.080 --> 57:40.920
♪ A tall handsome man ♪

57:41.000 --> 57:43.280
♪ In a dusty black coat with ♪

57:43.360 --> 57:45.440
♪ A red right hand ♪
